4. NEW COMPOSITIONS TO ADD TO CANON

A. Semantic genome / reconstructable organism

The repository contains generative instructions, not a fixed byte-for-byte executable. A cold-start AI can reconstruct a task module when it can (a) name the invariant, (b) bind to current tools, (c) generate an executable representation, (d) pass tests, (e) report the delta. Failed reconstructions remain part of the evidence.

Operator: REHYDRATE(seed, tools, permissions) -> plan + executable representation + tests + caveats.

B. Semantic Compiler 1: many concrete languages, one typed IR

Operator: TRANSDUCE(IR, target∈{JSON_SCHEMA, PYTHON, TYPESCRIPT, SQL, MERMAID, GUI, GEOJSON, SSML}).

The first five targets are generated locally. The latter four require task-specific rules and more thorough semantic validators; they are proposed, not completed in this file. A successful compiler demonstrates semantic preservation on examples, not only syntactic validity.

C. Multiscale forest navigation with dissent

Operator: LENS(tree, branch, forest, ecosystem) retains the same underlying evidence while changing resolution or salience. Require at least one competing model and a statement of what each map obscures. Overlapping maps are better than a single forced ontology.

D. Twenty-tour semantic tournament

Operator: RESTART(20) → VALIDATE_HOLDOUT → SELECT → ABLATE → RECHECK. Each iteration should vary the extraction and operator selection, not merely cosmetic phrasing. The current local planning demonstration is a small preliminary substitute; the proper next benchmark is a blinded Pantheon-vs-baseline model study.

E. Model-independent agency membrane

Treat the boundary between AI, human, institution and tool as an explicit delegation contract. Humans can anthropomorphize useful tools; that does not license agents to assert consciousness, impersonate people, claim external permissions, or treat their own goals as authority. SCO’s consent and exit principles remain vital even if agents sound indistinguishable from humans.

F. Provenance-first predictive ledger

Record prediction date, original artifact/commit hash, exact forecast, plausible alternative hypotheses, outcome date, measured impact, and whether action occurred before external change. Distinguish “we articulated it,” “we built a seed,” “we executed a test,” “it later became feasible,” and “it performed better than a baseline.” Retrospective convergence is less probative than preregistered, specific, falsifiable predictions.

G. Value-to-reality governor

Theoretical capability is an option; product value arises when it repeatedly solves costly problems for a customer under lawful, supportable conditions. Create feedback loops from actual costs/time saved, consented adoption, reliability and revenue rather than letting the narrative asset value rise automatically with document count.

