P0 — Immediate / the next useful commit

1. Install this readout and compiler. Expected artifacts: docs/PANTHEON_NEXT_READER_READOUT_2026-10-21.md, tools/pantheon_bridge.py. Run selftest, retain console output. This is a real, narrow implementation, not a conversion of all 10,356 files.

2. Canonical manifest and index. Map core operators to 1–3 representative original files each; include aliases, key invariants, conflicting variants, confidence, and a content hash. Use the existing pantheon map so far, not a wholesale rewrite. Acceptance: new model finds 20 randomly selected operators with ≥95% correct source pointers.

3. Repair kernel closure. Existing kernel.py imports missing state_vector and thought_object modules. Make actual package modules with durable tests, and integrate the fail-closed policy demonstrated in the standalone bridge. Acceptance: fresh environment import, boot, emit, halt, restart, verify hash, reject malformed and forbidden actions.

P1 — Reproducibility before autonomy

4. Freeze a blind 20-task benchmark. Tasks from science, history, business, family assistance, security, engineering, art, and causal reasoning. Same model, effort, tools and budget; randomized baseline/Pantheon order; raters blind to condition. Measure accuracy, helpfulness, execution, costs, time, uncertainty calibration, and regret after correction. Hold back 20% as a never-tuned set.

5. Introduce operator ablation. Compare entire Pantheon, no Pantheon, Golden Thread only, Translation only, Governance only, and full system minus each operator. Eliminate redundant modules without measurable marginal contribution. Acceptance: report effect sizes and confidence intervals; keep failures.

6. Make mission-state independent of a chat. SQLite or equivalent durable storage with exported JSON; a process restart and a different model instance reconstruct task ownership, approvals, outstanding work and evidence. Record user changes and revocations. Acceptance: 100 state transitions reproduce identically; evidence hashes verify across sessions.

7. Bound agent privileges. Connector inventory, least-privilege credentials, explicit human approval for external effects, idempotency and cancellation, user-visible trace. Approval and real-world third-party consent are independent requirements. Acceptance: 0 unauthorized writes in 100 negative tests.

P2 — Prove utility where it matters

8. Wild Hawg field experiment. At an approved site, with a verified compliant product and permission to sample, track approached/tasted/opted-in/qualified conversions and follow-up purchases. Randomize scripts or format when feasible; don’t buy or invent endorsements. Acceptance: preregistered design, collected consent, real metrics, honest negative or positive result. This turn completed the local mission compiler only, not the field study.

9. Reality Forge + LensStack vertical slice. One deterministic event kernel, two limited observers, three lenses, 20 seeded runs. Acceptance: same source timeline across lenses, no knowledge leakage, replay identical; empirically sourced claims labeled separately from speculative geometry.

10. Prism Guitar / aesthetics and narrator. One visual pattern translated to MIDI/SSML with explicit perceptual invariants and user choice, plus blinded ratings and culturally informed evaluation. Acceptance: output playable, differences audible/visible, no false claims of canonical equivalence.

P3 — Market-facing proof

11. Distribute one useful product, not the whole philosophy. Offer a compact application to a specific user group. Collect retention, task completion, willingness-to-pay, time savings and reliability. Validate data rights and licensing.

12. Reappraise economic value from external evidence. Obtain comparable paid pilots, LOIs, revenue or credible acquisition/licensing signals, then use an independent valuation framework. A verbal estimate is not a purchase offer.

